    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = x+yx^{3}, \left(2,5\right), \left(-5,-3\right), \left(-4,1\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(2,5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-5,-3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-4,1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>42</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>370</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-68</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(2,5\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(2,5) = 2  + 5(2)^{3} = 42</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-5,-3\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-5,-3) = -5   - 3(-5)^{3} = 370</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-4,1\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-4,1) = -4  + 1(-4)^{3} = -68</m>.


</solution>
